{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Dinah went out, etc.</b> The reason the verse says <b>daughter of Leah</b>, etc., is that Scripture intends to make known the causes that brought about her going out. They number three, and this is the construal of the verse: ״וַתֵּצֵא דִינָה״ — and the reason for her going out is on account of her being the daughter of Leah, for had she been the daughter of Rachel she would not have gone out; rather, it was because she was a daughter who went out (Genesis Rabbah 80:1) — Leah gave birth to her with this temperament and nature. Second cause: her being the only daughter of Jacob, one daughter among the sons. Further, her being the daughter of Jacob — this gave her a name and standing in the world, for through this Shechem did what he did, as I shall explain. The third: <b>to see the daughters of the land</b>, in the manner that our rabbis of blessed memory say (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 38) that Shechem brought the daughters of the land around Jacob's tent, and they were playing with musical instruments, etc., so that Dinah would go out to their sound — and this is a third cause for her going out. And from this you may infer that had Shechem not known about Dinah on account of her being the daughter of Jacob, who was renowned in the world and had a name through the birth of his sons, he would not have done his deed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:51.183699773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}